Switch to the correct audio profile

Linux uses two main Bluetooth audio profiles:

A2DP – High-quality stereo audio (music), no microphone.
HSP/HFP – Lower quality, but supports mic.

Discord usually wants the HSP/HFP profile if you want to use the AirPods mic. But AirPods Max’s HSP/HFP support on Linux is often unstable because Linux’s PulseAudio and BlueZ setup doesn’t fully handle Apple’s codec.

Check profiles using:

pactl list cards

Look for something like bluez_card.xx_xx_xx_xx_xx_xx and see which profiles are available.

Switch profiles with:

pavucontrol
Go to the Configuration tab.
Set your AirPods Max to either High Fidelity Playback (A2DP) for audio only or Headset Head Unit (HSP/HFP) for mic + audio.

⚠️ Note: HSP/HFP might be low quality or not work at all. A2DP is much more reliable.
